1
00:00:00,400 --> 00:00:06,412
Hello, and welcome to your maths paper one revision lesson. This is the non-calculator paper.

2
00:00:06,762 --> 00:00:10,185
We'll go through number, algebra, and ratio,

3
00:00:10,535 --> 00:00:13,958
then geometry, probability and statistics.

4
00:00:14,308 --> 00:00:19,960
For every topic, I'll show you what you need to know first, so that each rule makes sense.

5
00:00:20,310 --> 00:00:25,289
Get a pen and paper, and pause the video to try each example yourself.

6
00:00:26,039 --> 00:00:32,760
Let's start with negative numbers. Subtracting a negative is the same as adding. Five minus negative three is eight.

7
00:00:33,110 --> 00:00:41,571
When you multiply or divide, if the signs are the same, the answer is positive. Negative four times negative three is twelve.

8
00:00:41,921 --> 00:00:48,305
If the signs are different, the answer is negative. Negative four times three is negative twelve.

9
00:00:48,655 --> 00:00:58,197
The order of operations is BIDMAS: brackets, then indices, which means powers, then divide and multiply, then add and subtract.

10
00:00:58,547 --> 00:01:06,033
So, three plus four times two squared. Square first: four. Then multiply: sixteen. Then add: nineteen.

11
00:01:06,783 --> 00:01:14,467
No calculator, so we need written methods. For forty-seven times thirty-six, split each number into tens and ones.

12
00:01:14,817 --> 00:01:17,787
Multiply each part, like in the grid.

13
00:01:18,137 --> 00:01:22,269
Then add them up to get one thousand, six hundred and ninety-two.

14
00:01:22,619 --> 00:01:27,400
For decimals, ignore the decimal points first. Three times four is twelve.

15
00:01:27,750 --> 00:01:34,296
There are three decimal places in total in the question, so the answer is zero point zero one two.

16
00:01:34,646 --> 00:01:43,851
To divide by a decimal, multiply both numbers by ten. Six divided by zero point two becomes sixty divided by two, which is thirty.

17
00:01:44,601 --> 00:01:49,615
A prime number has exactly two factors: one and itself. One is not prime.

18
00:01:49,965 --> 00:01:54,421
Using a factor tree, sixty is two times two times three times five.

19
00:01:54,771 --> 00:01:58,659
And seventy-two is two times two times two times three times three.

20
00:01:59,009 --> 00:02:03,639
Put the shared primes, two, two and three, in the middle of a Venn diagram.

21
00:02:03,989 --> 00:02:07,459
The highest common factor is the product of the middle: twelve.

22
00:02:07,809 --> 00:02:12,404
The lowest common multiple is the product of everything: three hundred and sixty.

23
00:02:13,154 --> 00:02:19,457
The bottom of a fraction is the denominator. It says how many equal parts. The top is the numerator.

24
00:02:19,807 --> 00:02:25,064
To add two thirds and one quarter, the bottoms must be the same. Twelve works for both.

25
00:02:25,414 --> 00:02:30,672
Two thirds is eight twelfths. One quarter is three twelfths. Add the tops: eleven twelfths.

26
00:02:31,022 --> 00:02:38,984
With mixed numbers, change them to top-heavy fractions first. Two and a half is five halves. One and two thirds is five thirds.

27
00:02:39,334 --> 00:02:45,184
Make the bottoms six: fifteen sixths minus ten sixths is five sixths.

28
00:02:45,934 --> 00:02:53,467
To multiply, just multiply the tops and multiply the bottoms. Then simplify: six twentieths is three tenths.

29
00:02:53,817 --> 00:02:56,033
To divide, use KFC.

30
00:02:56,383 --> 00:02:59,864
Keep the first fraction. Flip the second one upside down.

31
00:03:00,214 --> 00:03:04,798
Change divide into times. Two times five is ten. Three times four is twelve.

32
00:03:05,148 --> 00:03:09,325
Simplify by dividing top and bottom by two: five sixths.

33
00:03:10,075 --> 00:03:13,452
Let's find thirty-five percent of two hundred and sixty.

34
00:03:13,802 --> 00:03:17,748
Ten percent is twenty-six. So thirty percent is seventy-eight.

35
00:03:18,098 --> 00:03:20,905
Five percent is half of ten percent: thirteen.

36
00:03:21,255 --> 00:03:22,763
Add them: ninety-one.

37
00:03:23,113 --> 00:03:32,341
A multiplier does it in one step. To increase by fifteen percent, times by one point one five. To decrease, times by zero point eight five.

38
00:03:33,091 --> 00:03:38,441
A coat costs sixty-eight pounds after fifteen percent off. What was the original price?

39
00:03:38,791 --> 00:03:44,571
Sixty-eight pounds is eighty-five percent of the original, because fifteen percent was taken off.

40
00:03:44,921 --> 00:03:50,260
So one percent is sixty-eight divided by eighty-five, which is zero point eight.

41
00:03:50,610 --> 00:03:53,336
And one hundred percent is eighty pounds.

42
00:03:53,686 --> 00:03:57,214
Compound interest is added on to the new total each year.

43
00:03:57,564 --> 00:04:04,099
Two hundred times one point one is two hundred and twenty. Times one point one again: two hundred and forty-two pounds.

44
00:04:04,849 --> 00:04:11,128
A power means repeated multiplication. Two to the power five is five twos multiplied together: thirty-two.

45
00:04:11,478 --> 00:04:16,898
When you multiply, add the powers. Three to the four times three squared is three to the six.

46
00:04:17,248 --> 00:04:19,579
When you divide, subtract the powers.

47
00:04:19,929 --> 00:04:22,308
A power of a power: multiply them.

48
00:04:22,658 --> 00:04:25,059
Anything to the power zero is one.

49
00:04:25,809 --> 00:04:31,937
A negative power means flip it. Two to the minus three is one over two cubed, which is one eighth.

50
00:04:32,287 --> 00:04:39,704
A fraction power means a root. Twenty-five to the power of a half is the square root of twenty-five, which is five.

51
00:04:40,054 --> 00:04:45,776
For eight to the power two thirds, the bottom, three, means cube root. The top, two, means square.

52
00:04:46,126 --> 00:04:49,526
The cube root of eight is two. Two squared is four.

53
00:04:49,876 --> 00:04:55,203
Now a hard one. Twenty-seven eighths to the power minus two thirds. The minus means flip it.

54
00:04:55,553 --> 00:04:59,278
Cube root both: two thirds. Then square: four ninths.

55
00:05:00,028 --> 00:05:08,025
Standard form is a short way to write big and small numbers. Forty-five thousand is four point five times ten to the four.

56
00:05:08,375 --> 00:05:16,408
Small numbers have a negative power. Zero point zero zero three six is three point six times ten to the minus three.

57
00:05:16,758 --> 00:05:21,748
To multiply, multiply the numbers and add the powers: twelve times ten to the nine.

58
00:05:22,098 --> 00:05:27,228
But twelve is not between one and ten. So it becomes one point two times ten to the ten.

59
00:05:27,978 --> 00:05:33,189
A surd is a square root that is not a whole number, like root two. We leave it as a root.

60
00:05:33,539 --> 00:05:42,012
To simplify, find the biggest square number factor. Root seventy-two is root thirty-six times root two, which is six root two.

61
00:05:42,362 --> 00:05:49,965
You can only add like surds. Root fifty is five root two. Root eighteen is three root two. Together, eight root two.

62
00:05:50,315 --> 00:05:57,430
To rationalise, remove the root from the bottom. Multiply top and bottom by root three. You get two root three.

63
00:05:57,780 --> 00:06:03,653
If the bottom is two plus root three, multiply top and bottom by two minus root three.

64
00:06:04,003 --> 00:06:09,423
The bottom becomes four minus three, which is one. So the answer is two minus root three.

65
00:06:10,173 --> 00:06:13,689
Let x equal zero point two seven recurring.

66
00:06:14,039 --> 00:06:17,439
Two digits repeat, so multiply by one hundred.

67
00:06:17,789 --> 00:06:24,880
Subtract the first line from the second. The recurring parts cancel out, leaving ninety-nine x equals twenty-seven.

68
00:06:25,230 --> 00:06:30,465
So x is twenty-seven over ninety-nine, which simplifies to three elevenths.

69
00:06:31,215 --> 00:06:35,114
To estimate, round every number to one significant figure.

70
00:06:35,464 --> 00:06:43,415
Forty-eight point seven becomes fifty. Three point one two becomes three. Zero point five one becomes zero point five.

71
00:06:43,765 --> 00:06:47,176
One hundred and fifty divided by a half is three hundred.

72
00:06:47,526 --> 00:06:58,078
A length is seven point four, to one decimal place. It could be as low as seven point three five, and up to, but not including, seven point four five.

73
00:06:58,828 --> 00:07:03,551
To expand a bracket, multiply everything inside by the term outside.

74
00:07:03,901 --> 00:07:08,729
For double brackets, multiply every term in the first by every term in the second.

75
00:07:09,079 --> 00:07:18,551
x times x is x squared. x times minus five is minus five x. Three times x is three x. Three times minus five is minus fifteen.

76
00:07:18,901 --> 00:07:23,172
Collect the x terms: x squared minus two x minus fifteen.

77
00:07:23,522 --> 00:07:28,675
Careful with squared brackets. Write it out twice. It is NOT x squared plus sixteen.

78
00:07:29,425 --> 00:07:34,020
Factorising is the opposite of expanding. First, take out common factors.

79
00:07:34,370 --> 00:07:39,500
For a quadratic, find two numbers that multiply to twelve and add to seven.

80
00:07:39,850 --> 00:07:44,121
Three and four. So it's x plus three, times x plus four.

81
00:07:44,471 --> 00:07:50,889
The difference of two squares: x squared minus forty-nine is x plus seven, times x minus seven.

82
00:07:51,239 --> 00:08:00,630
When there's a number in front of x squared, multiply a by c: six. Find two numbers that multiply to six and add to seven: six and one.

83
00:08:00,980 --> 00:08:07,375
Split the middle term and factorise in pairs. The answer is two x plus one, times x plus three.

84
00:08:08,125 --> 00:08:12,721
An equation is like a balance. Whatever you do to one side, do to the other.

85
00:08:13,071 --> 00:08:18,026
Take three x from both sides: four x plus three equals nineteen.

86
00:08:18,376 --> 00:08:22,171
Take three from both sides: four x equals sixteen.

87
00:08:22,521 --> 00:08:25,410
Divide by four: x equals four.

88
00:08:25,760 --> 00:08:31,482
With brackets, expand first. Then x minus six equals eight, so x equals fourteen.

89
00:08:32,232 --> 00:08:39,881
Rearranging works just like solving. Make x the subject of y equals three x minus two, all over five.

90
00:08:40,231 --> 00:08:42,690
Multiply both sides by five.

91
00:08:43,040 --> 00:08:44,710
Add two to both sides.

92
00:08:45,060 --> 00:08:46,568
Divide by three.

93
00:08:46,918 --> 00:08:52,419
If the letter appears twice, get both terms on one side, then factorise it out.

94
00:08:53,169 --> 00:08:58,508
The open sign means less than. With a line underneath, it means less than or equal to.

95
00:08:58,858 --> 00:09:05,566
On a number line, use an open circle for less than, and a filled circle for less than or equal to.

96
00:09:05,916 --> 00:09:12,126
Solve them like equations. Three x plus two is greater than fourteen, so x is greater than four.

97
00:09:12,476 --> 00:09:20,311
Five minus two x is less than or equal to eleven. Take five: minus two x is less than or equal to six.

98
00:09:20,661 --> 00:09:28,066
Divide by minus two, and flip the sign, because we divided by a negative. x is greater than or equal to minus three.

99
00:09:28,816 --> 00:09:31,693
The gap between terms is plus three every time.

100
00:09:32,043 --> 00:09:36,558
So the rule starts with three n. That gives three, six, nine, twelve.

101
00:09:36,908 --> 00:09:42,955
Our sequence is two more each time. So the nth term is three n plus two.

102
00:09:43,305 --> 00:09:47,993
Check: when n is one, three plus two is five. Correct.

103
00:09:48,343 --> 00:09:55,017
Is one hundred in the sequence? Solve three n plus two equals one hundred. n is not a whole number, so no.

104
00:09:55,367 --> 00:10:03,376
For a quadratic sequence, the second differences are the same. Halve that number to get the n squared term, then find the linear part.

105
00:10:04,126 --> 00:10:07,932
The equation of a straight line is y equals m x plus c.

106
00:10:08,282 --> 00:10:11,787
m is the gradient. It tells you how steep the line is.

107
00:10:12,137 --> 00:10:16,210
c is the y-intercept, where the line crosses the y-axis.

108
00:10:16,560 --> 00:10:22,317
The gradient is the change in y divided by the change in x. Up, divided by across.

109
00:10:22,667 --> 00:10:29,364
A line goes through one, five and three, eleven. Up six, across two, so the gradient is three.

110
00:10:29,714 --> 00:10:37,375
Put the point one, five into y equals three x plus c. Five equals three plus c, so c is two.

111
00:10:38,125 --> 00:10:40,491
Parallel lines have the same gradient.

112
00:10:40,841 --> 00:10:45,901
Perpendicular lines meet at a right angle. Their gradients multiply to minus one.

113
00:10:46,251 --> 00:10:51,218
To find it, flip the gradient and change the sign. Two becomes minus a half.

114
00:10:51,568 --> 00:10:54,132
Minus three quarters becomes four thirds.

115
00:10:54,482 --> 00:10:58,753
Always get y on its own first, so you can read the gradient.

116
00:10:59,503 --> 00:11:03,100
To solve a quadratic, first make it equal zero.

117
00:11:03,450 --> 00:11:08,255
Factorise it: x plus four, times x minus three.

118
00:11:08,605 --> 00:11:15,720
If two things multiply to zero, one of them must be zero. So x is minus four, or x is three.

119
00:11:16,070 --> 00:11:26,761
If it won't factorise, use the quadratic formula. x equals minus b, plus or minus the square root of b squared minus four a c, all over two a.

120
00:11:27,111 --> 00:11:34,168
For x squared plus four x plus one, that gives minus four, plus or minus root twelve, all over two.

121
00:11:34,518 --> 00:11:40,309
Root twelve is two root three. Divide by two: minus two, plus or minus root three.

122
00:11:41,059 --> 00:11:45,481
Completing the square. Take x squared plus six x plus two.

123
00:11:45,831 --> 00:11:50,090
Halve the six to get three. Write x plus three, squared.

124
00:11:50,440 --> 00:11:55,593
But that bracket makes an extra nine, so subtract nine. Then add the two.

125
00:11:55,943 --> 00:11:59,343
That gives x plus three, squared, minus seven.

126
00:11:59,693 --> 00:12:06,158
The turning point is minus three, minus seven. Change the sign inside the bracket, and keep the sign outside.

127
00:12:06,508 --> 00:12:12,021
On a graph, the roots, or solutions, are where the curve crosses the x-axis.

128
00:12:12,771 --> 00:12:17,053
Two equations, two unknowns. We want values that make both true.

129
00:12:17,403 --> 00:12:22,800
Both have plus two y. Same signs, so subtract the equations. Two x equals eight.

130
00:12:23,150 --> 00:12:24,727
So x equals four.

131
00:12:25,077 --> 00:12:30,230
Put that back in: four plus two y equals eight, so y equals two.

132
00:12:30,580 --> 00:12:34,850
Always check in the other equation. Twelve plus four is sixteen. Correct.

133
00:12:35,200 --> 00:12:41,967
If one equation is a quadratic, substitute the straight line equation into it, then solve the quadratic.

134
00:12:42,717 --> 00:12:48,764
A function is a rule. If f of x is three x minus one, then f of four is eleven.

135
00:12:49,114 --> 00:12:53,013
For f g of x, do g first, then f. Work from the right.

136
00:12:53,363 --> 00:12:56,856
For the inverse, rearrange to make x the subject.

137
00:12:57,206 --> 00:13:00,908
So f inverse of x is x plus one, all over three.

138
00:13:01,258 --> 00:13:09,092
Proof: three consecutive numbers add to three n plus three, which is three times something. So it's always a multiple of three.

139
00:13:09,842 --> 00:13:12,859
Share sixty pounds in the ratio three to two.

140
00:13:13,209 --> 00:13:15,425
First, add the parts: five.

141
00:13:15,775 --> 00:13:19,477
One part is sixty divided by five: twelve pounds.

142
00:13:19,827 --> 00:13:24,562
Three parts is thirty-six pounds, and two parts is twenty-four pounds.

143
00:13:24,912 --> 00:13:27,336
Check they add up to sixty. They do.

144
00:13:28,086 --> 00:13:34,969
y is directly proportional to x squared. y is thirty-six when x is three. Find y when x is five.

145
00:13:35,319 --> 00:13:39,741
Step one: write the equation with k. y equals k x squared.

146
00:13:40,091 --> 00:13:45,766
Step two: put in the numbers. Thirty-six equals nine k, so k is four.

147
00:13:46,116 --> 00:13:52,883
Step three: use it. When x is five, y is four times twenty-five, which is one hundred.

148
00:13:53,633 --> 00:13:58,286
A car travels one hundred and fifty kilometres in two and a half hours.

149
00:13:58,636 --> 00:14:03,499
Careful: two hours thirty minutes is two point five hours, not two point three.

150
00:14:03,849 --> 00:14:07,969
Speed is distance divided by time: sixty kilometres per hour.

151
00:14:08,319 --> 00:14:12,473
For area units, square the conversion. For volume units, cube it.

152
00:14:13,223 --> 00:14:19,444
Angles on a straight line add to one hundred and eighty degrees. Around a point, three hundred and sixty.

153
00:14:19,794 --> 00:14:24,367
Angles in a triangle add to one eighty. In a four-sided shape, three sixty.

154
00:14:24,717 --> 00:14:27,850
Vertically opposite angles, in an X shape, are equal.

155
00:14:28,200 --> 00:14:33,597
When you give reasons, write the full rule, like: alternate angles are equal.

156
00:14:34,347 --> 00:14:43,052
The interior angles of a polygon add to n minus two, times one eighty. That's because you can split it into n minus two triangles.

157
00:14:43,402 --> 00:14:49,147
A pentagon has five sides, so three triangles: five hundred and forty degrees.

158
00:14:49,497 --> 00:14:53,768
The exterior angles of any polygon add to three hundred and sixty.

159
00:14:54,118 --> 00:15:00,095
In a regular polygon, each exterior angle is three sixty divided by the number of sides.

160
00:15:00,445 --> 00:15:04,925
If the exterior angle is twenty degrees, there are eighteen sides.

161
00:15:05,675 --> 00:15:10,212
The area of a triangle is half times base times perpendicular height.

162
00:15:10,562 --> 00:15:15,193
A trapezium: add the parallel sides, halve it, times the height.

163
00:15:15,543 --> 00:15:22,786
A circle's area is pi r squared. Its circumference is two pi r, or pi times the diameter.

164
00:15:23,136 --> 00:15:30,936
With radius five, the area is twenty-five pi and the circumference is ten pi. On this paper, leave pi in.

165
00:15:31,286 --> 00:15:36,694
A sector is a fraction of a circle. Multiply the area by the angle over three sixty.

166
00:15:37,444 --> 00:15:43,503
A prism has the same shape all the way through. Its volume is the area of the cross-section times the length.

167
00:15:43,853 --> 00:15:47,554
A cylinder's volume is pi r squared h.

168
00:15:47,904 --> 00:15:51,629
A cone or pyramid is one third of the matching prism.

169
00:15:51,979 --> 00:15:55,553
A sphere's volume is four thirds pi r cubed.

170
00:15:56,303 --> 00:15:59,494
Pythagoras only works on right-angled triangles.

171
00:15:59,844 --> 00:16:03,848
The hypotenuse is the longest side, opposite the right angle.

172
00:16:04,198 --> 00:16:07,412
a squared plus b squared equals c squared.

173
00:16:07,762 --> 00:16:12,880
To find the longest side, add the squares. Six squared plus eight squared is one hundred.

174
00:16:13,230 --> 00:16:15,399
The square root of one hundred is ten.

175
00:16:15,749 --> 00:16:19,172
To find a shorter side, subtract instead.

176
00:16:19,522 --> 00:16:23,619
Learn these triples. They come up a lot on the non-calculator paper.

177
00:16:24,369 --> 00:16:32,923
Label the sides from the angle you're using. The hypotenuse is the longest. The opposite is across from the angle. The adjacent is next to it.

178
00:16:33,273 --> 00:16:35,988
Sine is opposite over hypotenuse.

179
00:16:36,338 --> 00:16:39,204
Cosine is adjacent over hypotenuse.

180
00:16:39,554 --> 00:16:42,072
Tangent is opposite over adjacent.

181
00:16:42,422 --> 00:16:47,993
The hypotenuse is ten, and the angle is thirty degrees. Find the opposite side.

182
00:16:48,343 --> 00:16:52,021
Sine of thirty is a half, so the opposite side is five.

183
00:16:52,771 --> 00:17:01,128
No calculator means you must know these. Sine thirty is a half. Cos thirty is root three over two. Tan thirty is root three over three.

184
00:17:01,478 --> 00:17:06,353
Sine and cos of forty-five are both root two over two. Tan forty-five is one.

185
00:17:06,703 --> 00:17:11,902
Sine sixty is root three over two. Cos sixty is a half. Tan sixty is root three.

186
00:17:12,252 --> 00:17:18,717
And sine zero is zero, sine ninety is one, cos zero is one, and cos ninety is zero.

187
00:17:19,067 --> 00:17:22,629
For any triangle, the area is a half a b sine C.

188
00:17:23,379 --> 00:17:27,093
The angle at the centre is twice the angle at the circumference.

189
00:17:27,443 --> 00:17:30,332
The angle in a semicircle is ninety degrees.

190
00:17:30,682 --> 00:17:33,095
Angles in the same segment are equal.

191
00:17:33,445 --> 00:17:37,379
Opposite angles in a cyclic quadrilateral add to one eighty.

192
00:17:37,729 --> 00:17:40,862
A tangent meets a radius at ninety degrees.

193
00:17:41,212 --> 00:17:45,006
Always write the theorem in your answer. That's where the marks are.

194
00:17:45,756 --> 00:17:50,619
To describe a rotation fully, give the angle, the direction, and the centre.

195
00:17:50,969 --> 00:17:54,705
For an enlargement, give the scale factor and the centre.

196
00:17:55,055 --> 00:17:58,281
Similar shapes are the same shape, different size.

197
00:17:58,631 --> 00:18:07,441
Two similar cylinders have heights four and twelve. The scale factor is three, so the volume scale factor is three cubed: twenty-seven.

198
00:18:07,791 --> 00:18:13,153
In vectors, to get from A to B, go back along a, then along b. That's b minus a.

199
00:18:13,903 --> 00:18:17,895
Probability goes from zero, impossible, to one, certain.

200
00:18:18,245 --> 00:18:23,468
A bag has three red and five blue balls. The probability of red is three out of eight.

201
00:18:23,818 --> 00:18:30,469
Probabilities add to one. If the chance of rain is zero point three, no rain is zero point seven.

202
00:18:30,819 --> 00:18:35,797
If you pick forty times, you'd expect three eighths of forty: fifteen reds.

203
00:18:36,147 --> 00:18:38,816
For AND, multiply. For OR, add.

204
00:18:39,566 --> 00:18:44,788
A bag has four red and three blue. Pick two, without putting the first one back.

205
00:18:45,138 --> 00:18:49,537
On the second pick, there's one ball fewer, so the bottoms become six.

206
00:18:49,887 --> 00:18:57,106
Multiply along the branches. Red then red is four sevenths times three sixths: twelve forty-seconds.

207
00:18:57,456 --> 00:19:02,238
Blue then blue is three sevenths times two sixths: six forty-seconds.

208
00:19:02,588 --> 00:19:07,265
Add the ends together: eighteen forty-seconds, which simplifies to three sevenths.

209
00:19:08,015 --> 00:19:12,692
In a Venn diagram, the symbol like an n means "and". It's the overlap.

210
00:19:13,042 --> 00:19:16,976
The symbol like a u means "or". It's everything in either circle.

211
00:19:17,326 --> 00:19:20,958
A with a dash means not A. Everything outside circle A.

212
00:19:21,308 --> 00:19:24,510
When you fill one in, always start with the middle.

213
00:19:24,860 --> 00:19:30,210
For A given B, only look inside circle B. Divide the overlap by the total in B.

214
00:19:30,960 --> 00:19:34,140
The mean is the total, divided by how many there are.

215
00:19:34,490 --> 00:19:37,959
The median is the middle value, once they're in order.

216
00:19:38,309 --> 00:19:42,266
The mode is the most common. The range is the biggest minus the smallest.

217
00:19:42,616 --> 00:19:50,266
From a frequency table, multiply each value by its frequency, add them up, and divide by the total frequency.

218
00:19:50,616 --> 00:19:57,649
When comparing two sets of data, compare an average and a spread, and say what it means in context.

219
00:19:58,399 --> 00:20:02,554
Scatter graphs show correlation: positive, negative or none.

220
00:20:02,904 --> 00:20:06,466
But correlation does not prove that one thing causes the other.

221
00:20:06,816 --> 00:20:11,098
On a cumulative frequency graph, read the median at half the total,

222
00:20:11,448 --> 00:20:18,134
and the quartiles at a quarter and three quarters. The interquartile range is upper quartile minus lower quartile.

223
00:20:18,484 --> 00:20:25,053
In a histogram, the height is frequency density. A group of width twenty with frequency forty has density two.

224
00:20:25,803 --> 00:20:32,756
Let's finish with exam tips. Always show your working. You get marks for method, even if the answer is wrong.

225
00:20:33,106 --> 00:20:39,443
Read every question twice. Look for words like exact, simplest form, and in terms of pi.

226
00:20:39,793 --> 00:20:41,579
Check your answer makes sense.

227
00:20:41,929 --> 00:20:45,050
And never leave a question blank. Write a first step.

228
00:20:45,400 --> 00:20:48,417
Well done for revising. Good luck in your mock!
